The algorithms, the numeric tables, the code generator that produces most of
the integral kernels, and the structure of this library are all libcint's.
This project translates them to Fortran and verifies, on every build, that the
translation produces bit-identical results.  It is not an independent
implementation and does not claim to be one.

PySCF
Copyright 2014- The PySCF Developers
https://github.com/pyscf/pyscf
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The effective core potential integrals -- src/cint_ecp_num.f90,
cint_ecp_ang.f90, cint_ecp_rad.f90, cint_ecp.f90 and cint_ecp_drv.f90, and the
ECPscalar entry points in cint_c_abi.f90 -- come from PySCF and not from
libcint, which has no ECP code.  They are a translation of
pyscf/lib/gto/nr_ecp.c and are verified against PySCF rather than against the
C this library otherwise ports.  The same licence applies; the copyright is a
different one, which is why it is named separately here.
